{"title":"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the smallest positive <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> squares of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4fa0f433944cff7a27b2875fe964297a992ee4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000 \\times 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" /> chessboard are colored, then there will exist three colored squares whose centers form a right triangle with sides parallel to the edges of the board.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd4f7a1059eb6f7423946b543e871ac55d3183c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest such number. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c284be1697c0caf56d0a39861380cec0605274e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\le 1998$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" />, we can simply color any of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9673ee04316e55d232ae3a9b8ce356386c0dc66a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1998$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> squares forming the top row and the left column, but excluding the top left corner square.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3be222417f4b1d5d32b8210ee0c3849714c5672a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] for(int i = 0; i &lt; 10; ++i){  for(int j = 0; j &lt; 10; ++j){   if((i == 0 || j == 9) &amp;&amp; !(j-i == 9)) fill(shift(i,j)*unitsquare,rgb(0.3,0.3,0.3));   else draw(shift(i,j)*unitsquare);  } } [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<p>We now show that no configuration with no colored right triangles exists for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd4f7a1059eb6f7423946b543e871ac55d3183c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. We call a row or column <i>filled</i> if all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> of its squares are colored. Then any of the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/0705411d92671faf1fe5602cfef8f353c7f0f83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> colored squares must share a column or row, respectively, with one of the colored squares in a filled row or column. These two squares, and any other square in the filled row or column, form a colored right triangle, giving us a contradiction. Hence, no filled row or column may exist.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of columns with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> colored square. Then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb198035c50c726516fd9a569ca6e5cc43eda5f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1999-m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> colored squares in the remaining columns, and in each of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968e9fc0d2731bef484380accf27ae628d91d1a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt; 1999-m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"93\" height=\"13\" /> columns that have a colored square must have at least two colored squares in them. These two colored squares will form a triangle with any other colored square in either of the rows containing the colored squares. Hence, each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb198035c50c726516fd9a569ca6e5cc43eda5f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1999-m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> colored squares must be placed in different rows, but as there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> rows, the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fb0fb00aa9531240cc5e96eb39fe924df84b50a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1999 - m \\le 1000 \\Longrightarrow m \\ge 999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"241\" height=\"15\" /> holds. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/7083ac815804c5915ca0e3cef398d8afd4b6be5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />, then each column only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> colored square, leaving no place for the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/0705411d92671faf1fe5602cfef8f353c7f0f83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, contradiction. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecda305f428bb146020256d8ef2bffd1ba5fb406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 999$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />, then each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> rows has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> black square, leaving no place for the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/0705411d92671faf1fe5602cfef8f353c7f0f83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, contradiction. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/0380dc53951a4c4267381a72a0cf07d9bd4b1da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{1999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"23\" /> is the minimal value.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>I claim that we can color at minimality 1999 squares and end up with one triangle whose legs are parallel to the sides of the chessboard.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 1:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6e6711991396b7eadb3a92753ca7bddb4ed54a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leq 1998$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> is impossible for all configurations of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> pieces.\n</p><p>Suppose one colors at maximum 1998 squares. From any configuration, there must never exist a configuration for which no such right triangle exists. However, one can color the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/900a7b0c32d4a4aef1f2beec3608e93fff88793a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999+999 = 1998$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" /> edge grids, exclusion of the corner, and now we show no right triangle is possible. Because the edges of the chessboard intersect at 90 degrees, the conjoined centres of the squares must also intersect at 90 degrees. Therefore, we can only form such a right triangle by using the corner piece. However, this was excluded from our original coloring. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4ecada300eb0f9179db98342f9946bc1653e501.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1998$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> does not work. Then, one may arrange all the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/0/8a011f963f8428e7b0a9f0c4ea458a649ab9c438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leq 1997$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> colored squares in the same configuration such that the corner piece is not colored whereas the edges are, and no such triangle can be formed by the centres. \n</p><p><b>Lemma 2:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd4f7a1059eb6f7423946b543e871ac55d3183c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> is possible for all configurations of the 1999 pieces.\n</p><p>We show that three pieces must form a right triangle whose sides are parallel to the grid. Suppose each distinct row obtains a colored piece. If we want to refute the claim, we put each of the 1000 squares on the diagonal, so now no two are shared. But now, no matter where we place the last colored piece, by the Pigeonhole Principle, this piece lies in the same row as another, and the same column as another. If we don't place the original 1000 squares on the diagonal, then at minimum two squares will be collinear. From there, we can place the 999 remaining squares anywhere, and by the Pigeonhole Principle, at least two pairs of squares share a common square that form a 90 degree triangle.\n</p><p><b>2000 USAMO/Q4:</b>\n</p><p>We must color a minimum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/0380dc53951a4c4267381a72a0cf07d9bd4b1da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{1999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"23\" /> squares.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO\" title=\"2000 USAMO\">2000 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017191820\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 207/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5837/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.167      1 -total\n 59.08%    8.370      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 39.26%    5.562      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7259:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017191820 and revision id 287671. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}